          "ruleId": "TM004",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "analytics-reader@acme-prod.iam.gserviceaccount.com: `examples/acme/workflows/payments-api/.github/workflows/pr-preview.yml#preview` runs on `pull_request_target` with id-token: write and checks out and runs pull request code, so anyone who can open a pull request controls a job that can mint this token. Its tokens carry the base branch `main`, which this trust accepts. Fix: Do not grant id-token: write to jobs triggered by pull_request_target, workflow_run or issue_comment. Run untrusted code in a `pull_request` job without cloud access, and deploy from a separate job on push to a protected branch, behind an environment with required reviewers."
